---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import TechGuide from "../components/TechGuide.astro";
---

<Layout title="Browser Storage Benchmark">
  <section class="hero-section">
    <h1>Browser Storage Benchmark</h1>
    <p>
      Analyze latency and compression efficiency performance of modern web
      browser storage technologies.
    </p>
    <div
      class="hero-actions"
      style="display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; justify-content: center; margin-top: 3rem;"
    >
      <a
        href="/storage?run=default"
        class="btn-primary-large"
        style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent-primary), var(--accent-secondary));"
      >
        ▶ Storage Benchmark
      </a>
      <a
        href="/compression?run=default"
        class="btn-primary-large"
        style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #a78bfa, #f472b6); border: none; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.4);"
      >
        ▶ Compression Benchmark
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="intro-section">
    <div class="section-divider">
      <span>Browser Storage &amp; Compression Guide</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-intro">
      <p>
        Modern browsers offer a diverse ecosystem of internal storage
        mechanisms. Selecting the optimal persistence strategy and compression
        algorithm tailored to your data's characteristics is critical for
        performance. Below is an overview of the various storage engines,
        wrapper libraries, and compression methodologies available within the
        browser environment.
      </p>
    </div>
    <TechGuide />
  </section>
</Layout>
